# Challenge70 (NewScenario22 topology) — VMware Vagrantfile
#
# Box swapped generic/ubuntu2204 -> bento/ubuntu-22.04, same version
# PROVISIONING already runs (202401.31.0). Validated end-to-end on
# Challenge130 first (same 5-router non-uniform mesh shape, r2r degree 4 on
# router-1, RIP, persist_boot_commands-based LAN/gateway addressing,
# network/traffic — all confirmed working, including full reboot-survival
# testing) before rolling out to this scenario.
#
# router-1 has r2r degree 4 (6 total adapters: NAT + mgmt + 4 r2r links) —
# same PCI-bridge slot overflow trigger seen on Challenge101/Challenge78 and
# confirmed to reproduce identically on bento (Challenge130's router-1 hit
# the exact same guest-eth-naming scramble). Not a new risk from this swap,
# and not something to hand-fix if it happens: network/resolve_iface_roles +
# fix_router_netplan.py already resolve it automatically via MAC-based
# reassignment (confirmed working on bento, zero code changes needed). If
# router-1 is unreachable via plain `ssh` while `vagrant ssh router-1` still
# works, that's this exact signature — check
# /etc/goad/iface-roles.env on router-1 rather than reaching for a manual fix.
#
# :networks order on each router MUST match that router's r2r_interfaces key
# order in ../../data/config.json — both are hand-maintained, nothing
# derives one from the other automatically.

